=== ANSWER A ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Read: {"file_path": "<home>/.claude/skills/caveman/SKILL.md"}
 - Bash: cat .git-blame-ignore-revs; echo ---; git ls-files | grep -vE '(^|/)(node_modules|package-lock\.json)' | grep -E '\.(js|json|md|yml|yaml|ts|html|ejs|css)$|^[^.]*$' | head -300 | wc -l
 - Bash: cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"; git ls-files | grep -vE 'package-lock|node_modules|\.(png|jpg|gif|ico|svg)$' > /tmp/files.txt; cat /tmp/files.txt | wc -l
while read f; do git blame -w -M -C --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs --line-porcelain HEAD -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -a '^author ' | sed 's/^author //'; done < /tmp/files.txt | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -25
echo --- total commits per author; git shortlog -sn HEAD | head -10
 - Bash: cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"; while read f; do git blame -w -M -C --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs --line-porcelain HEAD -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -a '^author ' | sed 's/^author //' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -1 | sed "s|^|$f: |"; done < /tmp/files.txt; git ls-files | xargs wc -l 2>/dev/null | tail -1
FINAL ANSWER:
Troy Goode owns the most surviving code, about 41% of lines. Douglas Christopher Wilson is second at about 32%.

I ran `git blame` on every tracked file at HEAD (19 files, about 2,000 lines). I used `-w -M -C` so whitespace changes and moved code don't count. I also passed `.git-blame-ignore-revs`, so the "reformat js with 4-space indent" commit doesn't take credit for every line.

The percentages are rounded from the top-25 line counts, so treat them as approximate.

| Author | Surviving lines | Share | Commits |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 810 | ~41% | 122 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 629 | ~32% | 143 |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 95 | ~5% | not in top 10 |
| Jon Church | 72 | ~4% | 3 |
| Sebastian Beltran | 67 | ~3% | not in top 10 |
| Ulises Gascón | 52 | ~3% | 3 |
| Ignacio Mangas | 44 | ~2% | 2 |
| Everyone else | each under 2% | ~10% | |

Ownership by area:
- **Troy Goode** owns the core and most of the tests. That is `lib/index.js` (159 lines, the library's only source file), `README.md`, and four of the five test files (`error-response.js`, `example-app.js`, `issue-2.js`, `vary.js`).
- **Douglas Wilson** owns the main test file `test/test.js` (339 lines), `package.json`, `HISTORY.md`, `LICENSE`, `ci.yml`, and the lint and ignore configs.
- **Íñigo Marquínez Prado, Sebastian Beltran and Ulises Gascón** own the GitHub workflow and dependabot files.

Wilson has more commits (143 vs 122) but fewer surviving lines. Much of his work edited or replaced existing lines, such as version bumps, `HISTORY.md` entries and config tweaks. Goode's original code mostly stayed.

The "top author per file" counts are the biggest contributor to each file, not the only one. `lib/index.js` also contains lines from Jon Church, Linus Unnebäck and others.
